 * tally. Pass 1 counts how often each record's id (u16 at +0x00) appears, using the
 * 0x78-byte scratch table at unk_20343E0 (30 slots of { u16 id; u16 count; }), which is
 * zero-filled first. Pass 2 stamps each record's reference id (low half of the word at
 * +0x14) with its tally count in the high half. Returns the number of records that had
 * a nonzero id. Both passes are do-while loops: the body runs once even when the record
 * count is 0, exactly as in the original. */
